{"descriptionModels":[{"description":"You have manifested an aberrant crystalmark. Determine its appearance and the flaw associated with it. You gain the following benefits:\n\n- Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n\n- You learn a cantrip of your choice from the warlock spell list. In addition, choose a 1st-level spell from the warlock spell list. You learn that spell and can cast it through your mark. Once you cast it, you must finish a short or long rest before you can cast it again through the mark. Constitution is your spellcasting ability for these spells.\n\n- Whenever you cast the 1st-spell, you can choose to cast it at a level equal to your proficiency bonus without requiring any components, regardless if you use a spell slot or not.\n\nYou also develop a random flaw from the Aberrant Crystalmark Flaws table.\n\nAberrant Crystalmark Flaws\nd8 --\u003e Flaw\n\n1 --\u003e Your mark is a source of constant physical pain.\n2 --\u003e Your mark whispers to you. Its meaning can be unclear.\n3 --\u003e When you\u0027re stressed, the mark hisses audibly.\n4 --\u003e The skin around the mark is burned, scaly, or withered.\n5 --\u003e Animals are uneasy around you.\n6 --\u003e You have a mood swing any time you use your mark.\n7 --\u003e Your looks change slightly whenever you use the mark.\n8 --\u003e You have horrific nightmares after you use your mark.","level":1},{"description":"You have manifested an aberrant crystalmark. Determine its appearance and the flaw associated with it. You gain the following benefits:\n\n- Increase your Constitution score by 1, to a maximum of 20.\n\n- You learn a cantrip of your choice from the warlock spell list. In addition, choose a 1st-level spell from the warlock spell list. You learn that spell and can cast it through your mark. Once you cast it, you must finish a short or long rest before you can cast it again through the mark. Constitution is your spellcasting ability for this 1st level which is cast at a level equal to your proficiency bonus.\n\n- Whenever you cast the 1st-spell, you can choose to cast it at a level equal to your proficiency bonus without requiring any components, regardless if you use a spell slot or not.\n\nYou also develop a random flaw from the Aberrant Crystalmark Flaws table.\n\nAberrant Crystalmark Flaws\nd8 --\u003e Flaw\n\n1 --\u003e Your mark is a source of constant physical pain.\n2 --\u003e Your mark whispers to you. Its meaning can be unclear.\n3 --\u003e When you\u0027re stressed, the mark hisses audibly.\n4 --\u003e The skin around the mark is burned, scaly, or withered.\n5 --\u003e Animals are uneasy around you.\n6 --\u003e You have a mood swing any time you use your mark.\n7 --\u003e Your looks change slightly whenever you use the mark.\n8 --\u003e You have horrific nightmares after you use your mark.\n\nOptional: Greater Aberrant Powers\n\nAt the GM\u0027s option, a character who has the Aberrant Crystalmark feat has a chance of manifesting greater power. Upon reaching 10th level, such a character has a 10 percent chance of increasing the power of this feat. If the character fails to gain a boon, they have an additional 10 percent chance the next time they gain a level. If the Destiny Points optional rule is available, it can be gained inmediatly by expending a Destiny Point.\n\nA character enhanced in this way can change the spell and cantrip choices made when it gained this feat. It can cast the 1st-spell at will instead of per short or long rest at a level equal to it\u0027s proficiency bonus. It also adds it\u0027s Constitution damage to the damage rolls of both the spell and cantrips if they deal damage. The spell can be cast once per turn freely whenever you would require an action, a bonus action or a reaction to do so.","level":10}],"id":"Custom4ac83e4b-7ff2-438b-a3b4-560a7e1bf42c","isFeature":false,"jsonType":"feat","level":1,"name":"Aberrant Crystalmark [SM]","notes":"","type":"Feat"}